jobs.description:
🌍 About the Company

Our client is an established banking and financial technology company
delivering specialized software solutions to banks and financial institutions across 80+ countries. Their platforms support critical financial transaction workflows and digital service channels used by global banking players.

💼 About the Role

As Head of Software Engineering
, you will lead the engineering team, ensure reliable delivery of mission-critical systems, and gradually strengthen engineering standards, architecture governance, and operational maturity.
This role combines people leadership, technical oversight and delivery accountability
.

🔍 Responsibilities:

Lead and develop a distributed software engineering team
while working full-time from the Vilnius office;
Ensure stable and predictable software delivery
aligned with business priorities;
Oversee backend architecture
based on microservices and server-based systems;
Strengthen SDLC processes, CI/CD pipelines and quality assurance practices
;
Establish and maintain engineering standards, documentation, and code quality guidelines;
Plan engineering capacity and support hiring and team development;
Collaborate closely with Product and stakeholders to translate requirements into scalable solutions;
Support infrastructure and deployment practices in Kubernetes-based environments;
Act as a senior technical reference point when needed (Java or .NET ecosystem);
Foster knowledge-sharing, documentation culture, and domain ownership within the team.

🎓 Requirements:

Proven experience as an Engineering Manager, Team Lead
or similar role;
Strong hands-on background in backend development
(Java or .NET);
Solid experience with microservices and server-based architectures;

Proven experience improving SDLC processes, CI/CD pipelines, and engineering quality practices
in production environments;
Experience in FinTech, banking, payments or other regulated environments;
Practical experience working with Kubernetes in production environments;
Strong leadership and communication skills;
Fluency in Russian and English
(spoken and written).

Nice to Have:

Experience improving engineering processes and team performance;
Familiarity with DevOps best practices and infrastructure automation;
Experience introducing documentation standards (e.g., ADRs, system design documentation);
Experience working with high-availability or mission-critical systems;
Lithuanian language skills.

🤝 Key Competencies:

Strong people leadership and team development skills
;
Strong technical and architectural judgement;
Delivery and results-oriented mindset;
Strong problem-solving and decision-making skills;
Effective cross-functional communication and collaboration.

✨ The Employer offers:

Senior leadership role with real ownership over engineering delivery;

Opportunity to shape
engineering standards and team growth;
Stable, long-term product environment;

Competitive compensation aligned with senior engineering leadership benchmarks; monthly salary €5,000 - €7,500;
Professional and pragmatic work culture;
Full-time office-based role in Vilnius.

If you’re ready to lead engineers, shape scalable systems, and take responsibility for both people and technology – let’s talk.

